      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start. Can you expand on the section about ergonomics and physical discomfort? Maybe include some specific details on how to identify early signs of strain or what those small, nagging aches might feel like in the wrists or neck, so people know when to take it seriously.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To expand on physical discomfort, you should detail the subtle signs of strain, which often start as minor annoyances before becoming serious issues. For wrists, mention tingling, numbness, or a dull ache during prolonged typing sessions. Neck and shoulder strain might manifest as tightness, stiffness, or a persistent headache that seems unrelated to stress. Encourage them to listen to their bodies, as these early signals are the best warning signs to adjust their setup or take a short break.",
      "source": "target",
