      "content": "Here is a draft memo for your review. It aims for a supportive, professional tone while using engaging language to address the risks.\n\n***\n\n**Subject: Keeping Our Remote Workspaces Healthy: A Quick Guide to Ergonomics**\n\nHi Team,\n\nAs we continue to thrive in our remote environment, your health and comfort are our top priorities. We want to ensure that your home workspace supports your productivity, not hinders it. Just like a well-maintained tool, your workstation needs proper setup to prevent strain, which can sneak up on you if you aren't mindful.\n\nTo keep those nagging aches at bay, please review these key ergonomic tips:\n\n*   **Posture Power:** Ensure your chair supports your lower back, and your monitor is positioned so the top third of the screen is at eye level. Think of your setup as being as stable as a well-built piece of furniture—not a pile of mismatched gear.\n*   **Wrist & Neck Watch:** Pay attention to small signals. Are your wrists tingling after a long meeting? Is your neck feeling stiff by mid-afternoon? These early signs are your body’s way of saying, \"Hey, take a breather!\"\n*   **The Break Ritual:**",
      "source": "target",
